<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bos taurus Gierer–Meinhardt wavelength at 3.137 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Bos taurus)",
        "Bos taurus Gierer–Meinhardt wavelength at 3.137 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Bos taurus morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Bos taurus specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Bos taurus" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim Holstein flank patches are a Turing pattern. That is a different script and a different scale.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a second animal or a scale-barred skin section. Both are open remediation.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the last GIF frame is a micrograph. It is the voucher photograph blended with the activator so the image-fitness crop can see both.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Dimensionless Gierer–Meinhardt integration on a 128^2 periodic grid, length-calibrated so the fastest-growing mode is 3.137 µm at diffusion scale s = 1.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: FFT wavelength versus k_star(s) over nine scales (Pearson r = 0.99595), equal-diffusion and production-off controls, and border-contrast segmentation of one Hereford calf photograph.",
        "reported_in_source: Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) published short-range activation and long-range inhibition with the activator–inhibitor kinetics implemented here.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived diffusion-driven instability and the dispersion relation whose fastest mode sets a wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Wasmeier et al. (2008) review melanosomes as sub-micrometre organelles. Murray (1981) proposed a macroscopic coat pre-pattern, which this slot does not re-test.",
        "transfer_boundary: Chronoseries length is 1. Nothing in the run estimates a domestication-driven change in wavelength, because no predecessor age is in the slot.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 3.137 µm assignment is a scale-tier detail wavelength, not a length read off the calf portrait. The portrait does not resolve 3 µm." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/bos_taurus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Bos taurus; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived diffusion-driven instability and the dispersion relation whose fastest mode sets a wavelength. | Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) published short-range activation and long-range inhibition with the activator–inhibitor kinetics implemented here. | Wasmeier et al. (2008) review melanosomes as sub-micrometre organelles. Murray (1981) proposed a macroscopic coat pre-pattern, which this slot does not re-test.; reconstructed_in_script: Dimensionless Gierer–Meinhardt integration on a 128^2 periodic grid, length-calibrated so the fastest-growing mode is 3.137 µm at diffusion scale s = 1. | FFT wavelength versus k_star(s) over nine scales (Pearson r = 0.99595), equal-diffusion and production-off controls, and border-contrast segmentation of one Hereford calf photograph.; transfer_boundary: The 3.137 µm assignment is a scale-tier detail wavelength, not a length read off the calf portrait. The portrait does not resolve 3 µm. | Chronoseries length is 1. Nothing in the run estimates a domestication-driven change in wavelength, because no predecessor age is in the slot.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Holstein flank patches are a Turing pattern. That is a different script and a different scale. | Does not claim the last GIF frame is a micrograph. It is the voucher photograph blended with the activator so the image-fitness crop can see both. | Does not claim a second animal or a scale-barred skin section. Both are open remediation.]; phenomenon_size: 9.5 mm (0.00946 m, log10=-2.024 m, tier=6_organ_mm); species_scale_ladder (2 runs from 9.5 mm to 50 cm): 9.5 mm:airway-mucosal-creasing, 50 cm:bos-taurus-turing-wavelength" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/jcs.040667> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-10>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-9> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Reaction-Diffusion & Turing Dispersion" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 8.56e-01 .

